<h1>Event Management for Teams & Clubs</h1>

<p class="lead">Event management for teams and clubs that handles RSVPs, volunteer shifts, check-in, and time tracking in one calendar — not four disconnected tools.</p>

<img src="/images/ss-calendar.png" alt="GatherPack calendar screenshot showing events with RSVPs and shift sign-ups" width="827" height="827" loading="lazy" style="width:100%;max-width:560px;height:auto;display:block;margin:0 auto;" class="rounded border">

<section id="overview" class="card" aria-labelledby="overview-heading">
  <div class="card-header">
    <h2 id="overview-heading">One calendar everyone can find</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="card-body">
    <p>Post meetings, practices, competitions, or gatherings in a single place. Members RSVP, sign up for shifts, and check in without you chasing forms and group chats. Events belong to teams, so people only see what matters to them — a youth club sees its rehearsals, a robotics team sees build season, and leaders see the whole picture in one view.</p>
    <p class="mb-0">If you already use Google Calendar, that sync is actively on the <a href="/roadmap/">roadmap</a> — we kept it as a planned integration rather than pretending it’s done.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="capabilities" class="card" aria-labelledby="capabilities-heading">
  <div class="card-header">
    <h2 id="capabilities-heading">What you can do</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="card-body">
    <div class="row g-4">

      <div class="col-12 col-md-6 col-lg-4 d-flex">
        <div class="feature-card w-100">
          <div class="feature-card__icon">
            <i class="fa-4x fa-solid fa-calendar-check" aria-hidden="true"></i>
          </div>
          <div class="feature-card__body">
            <h3>RSVP &amp; custom fields</h3>
            <p>Let people RSVP and capture what your event requires — hotel assignments, t-shirt sizes, transportation, or any custom field you define.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="col-12 col-md-6 col-lg-4 d-flex">
        <div class="feature-card w-100">
          <div class="feature-card__icon">
            <i class="fa-4x fa-solid fa-people-group" aria-hidden="true"></i>
          </div>
          <div class="feature-card__body">
            <h3>Shifts &amp; check-in</h3>
            <p>Offer volunteer shift sign-ups and track attendance at specific checkpoints during longer events. Requirements before check-in are on the roadmap.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="col-12 col-md-6 col-lg-4 d-flex">
        <div class="feature-card w-100">
          <div class="feature-card__icon">
            <i class="fa-4x fa-solid fa-clock" aria-hidden="true"></i>
          </div>
          <div class="feature-card__body">
            <h3>Time clock &amp; kiosk</h3>
            <p>Log volunteer hours through a kiosk with PIN, barcode, or RFID. Create multiple time-clock periods to report by activity, not just by date.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
    <p class="mt-3 mb-0 small text-muted">Also tracking birthdays? GatherPack keeps those visible so you don't need a separate list. See <a href="/features/members/">member management</a> for how rosters power the calendar.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="related" class="card" aria-labelledby="related-heading">
  <div class="card-header">
    <h2 id="related-heading">Connected to everything else</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="card-body">
    <p>Events feed directly into time tracking and reporting — log hours in the kiosk, then pull attendance trends in <a href="/features/automation/">custom reports</a>. Because events are tied to <a href="/features/members/">teams</a>, <a href="/features/communication/">announcements</a> and <a href="/features/finance/">finance entries</a> can stay scoped to the right people without extra bookkeeping.</p>
    <p class="mb-0">Use cases that lean on events: <a href="/use-cases/first-robotics/">FIRST Robotics</a> (build season + competition logistics), <a href="/use-cases/sports-leagues/">sports leagues</a> (practices, games, volunteer slots), <a href="/use-cases/nonprofits/">nonprofits</a> (community service days). Browse sibling pillars: <a href="/features/members/">Members</a> · <a href="/features/finance/">Finance</a> · <a href="/features/communication/">Communication</a> · <a href="/features/automation/">Automation</a></p>
  </div>
</section>

